# Spanish A2 — elementary vocabulary
# Format: word | translations (semicolon-separated) | example sentence | category | difficulty (1-5) | example in English
# Examples: short and everyday, and they contain the word exactly as listed. Past tenses,
# ir a + infinitive, object pronouns and comparatives are fine at A2.
# Neutral, Latin-American-friendly Spanish; where Spain uses another word, the translation says so.
# No word here repeats A1 (a1.psv or the A1 lessons' words) or B1-C2.

# Travel and holidays
viaje | trip; journey | El viaje en autobús duró tres horas. | travel | 2 | The bus trip took three hours.
maleta | suitcase | Anoche hice la maleta para el viaje. | travel | 2 | Last night I packed my suitcase for the trip.
vacaciones | vacation; holidays | Tomo dos semanas de vacaciones en agosto. | travel | 2 | I take two weeks of vacation in August.
reservar | to book; to reserve | Tenemos que reservar el hotel esta semana. | travel | 3 | We have to book the hotel this week.
reserva | reservation; booking (in Mexico also: reservación) | Hice la reserva del hotel por internet. | travel | 3 | I made the hotel reservation online.
habitación doble | double room | Quisiera una habitación doble para tres noches. | travel | 3 | I'd like a double room for three nights.
habitación individual | single room (also: habitación sencilla) | ¿Tienen una habitación individual para esta noche? | travel | 3 | Do you have a single room for tonight?
alojamiento | accommodation; lodging; place to stay | Encontramos un alojamiento barato cerca de la playa. | travel | 3 | We found a cheap place to stay near the beach.
huésped | guest (at a hotel or in a home) | Cada huésped recibe una toalla y una llave. | travel | 4 | Each guest gets a towel and a key.
pasaporte | passport | Mi pasaporte vence en marzo. | travel | 2 | My passport expires in March.
frontera | border | Cruzamos la frontera en autobús. | travel | 3 | We crossed the border by bus.
extranjero | abroad; foreigner; foreign | Mi tía trabaja en el extranjero. | travel | 3 | My aunt works abroad.
excursión | trip; outing; excursion | Ayer hicimos una excursión a la montaña. | travel | 2 | Yesterday we went on a trip to the mountains.
visitar | to visit | Mañana vamos a visitar a mis abuelos. | travel | 2 | Tomorrow we're going to visit my grandparents.
guía | guide; guidebook | El guía nos contó la historia del castillo. | travel | 2 | The guide told us the history of the castle.
castillo | castle | El verano pasado visitamos un castillo en España. | travel | 2 | Last summer we visited a castle in Spain.
monumento | monument | El monumento más famoso está en la plaza. | travel | 3 | The most famous monument is in the square.
capital | capital (city) | Lima es la capital de Perú. | travel | 2 | Lima is the capital of Peru.
lugar | place | Este es mi lugar favorito de la ciudad. | travel | 2 | This is my favorite place in the city.
vista | view | Desde el hotel hay una vista increíble del mar. | travel | 2 | From the hotel there's an amazing view of the sea.
acampar | to camp; to go camping | El verano pasado fuimos a acampar al lago. | travel | 3 | Last summer we went camping at the lake.
tomar el sol | to sunbathe | Me encanta tomar el sol en la playa. | travel | 2 | I love sunbathing on the beach.
postal | postcard | Les mandé una postal a mis abuelos. | travel | 2 | I sent my grandparents a postcard.
seguro | safe; sure | Este barrio es muy seguro de noche. | travel | 2 | This neighborhood is very safe at night.
peligroso | dangerous | Es peligroso nadar cuando hay olas grandes. | travel | 3 | It's dangerous to swim when there are big waves.
antiguo | old; ancient; former | La catedral es el edificio más antiguo de la ciudad. | travel | 3 | The cathedral is the oldest building in the city.

# Transport and getting around
girar | to turn | En el semáforo tienes que girar a la izquierda. | transportation | 2 | At the traffic light you have to turn left.
cruzar | to cross | Hay que cruzar la calle con cuidado. | transportation | 2 | You have to cross the street carefully.
esquina | corner | Te espero en la esquina de mi calle. | transportation | 2 | I'll wait for you on the corner of my street.
semáforo | traffic light | Espera, el semáforo está en rojo. | transportation | 3 | Wait, the traffic light is red.
parada | stop (bus, tram) | Me bajo en la próxima parada. | transportation | 2 | I get off at the next stop.
subir | to get on; to go up | Vamos a subir al tren. | transportation | 2 | We're going to get on the train.
bajar | to get off; to go down | Tenemos que bajar en la próxima estación. | transportation | 2 | We have to get off at the next station.
pasajero | passenger | Cada pasajero puede llevar una maleta. | transportation | 2 | Each passenger can bring one suitcase.
asiento | seat | Mi asiento está al lado de la ventana. | transportation | 2 | My seat is next to the window.
ida y vuelta | round trip; return (ticket) | Compré un boleto de ida y vuelta. | transportation | 3 | I bought a round-trip ticket.
aterrizar | to land | El avión va a aterrizar en diez minutos. | transportation | 3 | The plane is going to land in ten minutes.
transporte | transportation; transport | El transporte público aquí es muy bueno. | transportation | 2 | Public transportation here is very good.
conducir | to drive (in much of Latin America: manejar) | Mi madre me está enseñando a conducir. | transportation | 2 | My mother is teaching me to drive.
manejar | to drive (Latin America; in Spain: conducir) | Mi abuelo ya no puede manejar. | transportation | 2 | My grandfather can't drive anymore.
licencia de conducir | driver's license (in Spain: carné de conducir) | Mi hermano sacó la licencia de conducir a los dieciocho. | transportation | 3 | My brother got his driver's license at eighteen.
carretera | road; highway | La carretera estaba cerrada por la nieve. | transportation | 3 | The road was closed because of the snow.
autopista | highway; freeway; motorway | Tomamos la autopista para llegar antes. | transportation | 3 | We took the highway to get there sooner.
puente | bridge | Cruzamos el puente a pie. | transportation | 2 | We crossed the bridge on foot.
gasolina | gas; gasoline; petrol (in Argentina: nafta) | La gasolina subió mucho este año. | transportation | 3 | Gas went up a lot this year.
estacionamiento | parking lot; parking; car park (in Spain: aparcamiento) | El estacionamiento del hotel es gratis. | transportation | 3 | The hotel parking is free.
accidente | accident | Ayer hubo un accidente en la autopista. | transportation | 2 | Yesterday there was an accident on the highway.
multa | fine; ticket | La policía le puso una multa a mi tío. | transportation | 3 | The police gave my uncle a ticket.
rápido | fast; quick | El tren es más rápido que el autobús. | transportation | 2 | The train is faster than the bus.
lento | slow | Este autobús es muy lento. | transportation | 2 | This bus is very slow.
lleno | full | El metro iba lleno esta mañana. | transportation | 2 | The subway was full this morning.
último | last | Perdimos el último tren a casa. | transportation | 2 | We missed the last train home.

# Restaurants and cooking
menú | menu | ¿Nos trae el menú, por favor? | food | 2 | Could you bring us the menu, please?
propina | tip | Le dejamos una buena propina al mesero. | food | 3 | We left the waiter a good tip.
cuchillo | knife | Necesito un cuchillo para cortar la carne. | food | 2 | I need a knife to cut the meat.
servilleta | napkin | ¿Me pasas una servilleta, por favor? | food | 3 | Can you pass me a napkin, please?
taza | cup; mug | Tomé una taza de chocolate caliente. | food | 2 | I had a cup of hot chocolate.
botella | bottle | Pedimos una botella de agua para la mesa. | food | 2 | We ordered a bottle of water for the table.
mismo | same | Siempre pido el mismo plato aquí. | food | 2 | I always order the same dish here.
vegetariano | vegetarian | ¿Tienen algún plato vegetariano? | food | 3 | Do you have any vegetarian dishes?
delicioso | delicious | El pastel de mi abuela estaba delicioso. | food | 2 | My grandmother's cake was delicious.
rico | tasty; delicious; rich | Este arroz está muy rico. | food | 2 | This rice is really tasty.
picante | spicy; hot | Esta salsa es demasiado picante para mí. | food | 2 | This sauce is too spicy for me.
salado | salty; savory | El jamón es muy salado. | food | 3 | The ham is very salty.
dulce | sweet | No me gusta el café muy dulce. | food | 2 | I don't like my coffee very sweet.
cortar | to cut | ¿Me ayudas a cortar las verduras? | food | 2 | Can you help me cut the vegetables?
freír | to fry | Mi papá va a freír el pescado. | food | 3 | My dad is going to fry the fish.
hornear | to bake | Vamos a hornear galletas este fin de semana. | food | 3 | We're going to bake cookies this weekend.
horno | oven | El pan todavía está en el horno. | food | 3 | The bread is still in the oven.
aceite | oil | Pon un poco de aceite en la sartén. | food | 2 | Put a little oil in the frying pan.
mantequilla | butter | Me gusta el pan con mantequilla. | food | 2 | I like bread with butter.
jamón | ham | Desayuné un sándwich de jamón y queso. | food | 2 | I had a ham and cheese sandwich for breakfast.
cebolla | onion | No me gusta la cebolla cruda. | food | 2 | I don't like raw onion.
zanahoria | carrot | El conejo se comió una zanahoria. | food | 2 | The rabbit ate a carrot.
frijoles | beans (in Spain: judías or alubias) | Comimos arroz con frijoles. | food | 2 | We had rice and beans.
limón | lemon; lime | Me gusta el agua con limón. | food | 2 | I like water with lemon.
fresa | strawberry (in parts of South America: frutilla) | Mi helado favorito es de fresa. | food | 2 | My favorite ice cream is strawberry.

# Clothes
abrigo | coat | No olvides el abrigo, hace mucho frío. | clothing | 2 | Don't forget your coat, it's very cold.
chaqueta | jacket | Ponte la chaqueta, hace frío. | clothing | 2 | Put your jacket on, it's cold.
bufanda | scarf | Mi abuela me hizo una bufanda de lana. | clothing | 2 | My grandmother made me a wool scarf.
guantes | gloves | Perdí los guantes en el autobús. | clothing | 2 | I lost my gloves on the bus.
zapatillas | sneakers; trainers (in Mexico: tenis) | Necesito zapatillas nuevas para correr. | clothing | 2 | I need new sneakers for running.
jeans | jeans (in Spain: vaqueros) | Me compré unos jeans negros. | clothing | 2 | I bought some black jeans.
blusa | blouse | Mi mamá lleva una blusa blanca. | clothing | 2 | My mom is wearing a white blouse.
traje | suit | Mi hermano se puso un traje para la boda. | clothing | 3 | My brother put on a suit for the wedding.
traje de baño | swimsuit; swimming trunks (in Spain also: bañador) | No olvides el traje de baño para la piscina. | clothing | 3 | Don't forget your swimsuit for the pool.
cinturón | belt | Este pantalón me queda grande, necesito un cinturón. | clothing | 3 | These pants are too big for me, I need a belt.
bolsillo | pocket | Tengo las llaves en el bolsillo. | clothing | 3 | I have the keys in my pocket.
reloj | watch; clock | Mi abuelo me regaló un reloj. | clothing | 2 | My grandfather gave me a watch.
lentes | glasses (in Spain: gafas); lenses | Mi abuela no puede leer sin lentes. | clothing | 3 | My grandmother can't read without glasses.
algodón | cotton | Esta camiseta es de algodón. | clothing | 3 | This T-shirt is cotton.
moda | fashion | Esos zapatos están de moda este año. | clothing | 3 | Those shoes are in fashion this year.
talla | size (clothes) | ¿Tiene esta camisa en otra talla? | clothing | 3 | Do you have this shirt in another size?
probador | fitting room (in some countries: vestidor) | El probador está al fondo de la tienda. | clothing | 3 | The fitting room is at the back of the store.
probarse | to try on | Mi hermana quiere probarse el vestido azul. | clothing | 3 | My sister wants to try on the blue dress.
quedar | to fit; to suit; to look (on someone) | Esa camisa te va a quedar muy bien. | clothing | 3 | That shirt is going to look really good on you.
apretado | tight | Este pantalón me queda apretado. | clothing | 3 | These pants are tight on me.
cómodo | comfortable | Este suéter es muy cómodo. | clothing | 2 | This sweater is very comfortable.
ponerse | to put on (clothes) | Mi papá va a ponerse la corbata roja. | clothing | 3 | My dad is going to put on the red tie.
quitarse | to take off (clothes) | Aquí hay que quitarse los zapatos. | clothing | 3 | Here you have to take off your shoes.

# Shops and money
costar | to cost | ¿Cuánto va a costar el envío? | shopping | 2 | How much is shipping going to cost?
descuento | discount | Hay un descuento del veinte por ciento. | shopping | 3 | There's a twenty percent discount.
rebajas | sales | Compré estos zapatos en las rebajas. | shopping | 3 | I bought these shoes in the sales.
caja | checkout; cash register; box | Hay que pagar en la caja. | shopping | 2 | You have to pay at the checkout.
fila | line; queue (in Spain: cola) | Había una fila muy larga en la caja. | shopping | 2 | There was a very long line at the checkout.
recibo | receipt | Guarda el recibo por si quieres devolver la camisa. | shopping | 3 | Keep the receipt in case you want to return the shirt.
efectivo | cash | Prefiero pagar en efectivo. | shopping | 3 | I prefer to pay in cash.
tarjeta de crédito | credit card | ¿Puedo pagar con tarjeta de crédito? | shopping | 2 | Can I pay by credit card?
cajero automático | ATM; cash machine | ¿Hay un cajero automático por aquí? | shopping | 3 | Is there an ATM around here?
cambio | change (money); exchange | No tengo cambio para el autobús. | shopping | 2 | I don't have change for the bus.
moneda | coin; currency | Encontré una moneda en la calle. | shopping | 2 | I found a coin in the street.
ahorrar | to save (money) | Quiero ahorrar para comprar una bicicleta. | shopping | 3 | I want to save up to buy a bike.
devolver | to return (something); to give back | Quiero devolver estos zapatos. | shopping | 3 | I want to return these shoes.
cliente | customer; client | El cliente pidió otra talla. | shopping | 2 | The customer asked for another size.
marca | brand | ¿De qué marca es tu celular? | shopping | 2 | What brand is your phone?
gratis | free (no cost) | La entrada al museo es gratis los domingos. | shopping | 2 | Entrance to the museum is free on Sundays.
abierto | open | El supermercado está abierto hasta las diez. | shopping | 2 | The supermarket is open until ten.
cerrado | closed | El banco está cerrado los domingos. | shopping | 2 | The bank is closed on Sundays.
centro comercial | shopping mall; shopping center | Fuimos al centro comercial el sábado. | shopping | 2 | We went to the mall on Saturday.
panadería | bakery | Compro el pan en la panadería de la esquina. | shopping | 2 | I buy bread at the bakery on the corner.
librería | bookstore; bookshop | Compré este libro en una librería pequeña. | shopping | 3 | I bought this book in a small bookstore.
kilo | kilo; kilogram | Quiero un kilo de tomates, por favor. | shopping | 2 | I'd like a kilo of tomatoes, please.
paquete | package; parcel; packet | Llegó un paquete para ti. | shopping | 2 | A package arrived for you.

# Health and the body
salud | health | La salud es lo más importante. | health | 2 | Health is the most important thing.
dolor | pain; ache | Tengo un dolor muy fuerte en la rodilla. | health | 2 | I have a really bad pain in my knee.
dolor de cabeza | headache | Tengo un dolor de cabeza muy fuerte. | health | 2 | I have a really bad headache.
doler | to hurt; to ache | Después del partido me empezó a doler la pierna. | health | 3 | After the game my leg started to hurt.
fiebre | fever; temperature | Anoche tuve fiebre alta. | health | 2 | Last night I had a high fever.
tos | cough | Tengo tos desde el lunes. | health | 2 | I've had a cough since Monday.
gripe | flu (in Colombia and Mexico also: gripa) | Mi hermano tiene gripe y no fue a la escuela. | health | 2 | My brother has the flu and didn't go to school.
resfriado | cold (illness) | Tengo un resfriado muy fuerte. | health | 3 | I have a bad cold.
alergia | allergy | Tengo alergia a los gatos. | health | 3 | I'm allergic to cats.
herida | wound; injury | La herida no es profunda. | health | 3 | The wound isn't deep.
grave | serious | El accidente no fue grave. | health | 3 | The accident wasn't serious.
enfermedad | illness; disease | La gripe es una enfermedad muy común. | health | 3 | The flu is a very common illness.
enfermarse | to get sick (in Spain: ponerse enfermo) | Es fácil enfermarse cuando hace frío. | health | 3 | It's easy to get sick when it's cold.
sentirse | to feel | Es normal sentirse cansado después de un viaje. | health | 3 | It's normal to feel tired after a trip.
sano | healthy | Es importante comer sano. | health | 2 | It's important to eat healthily.
medicamento | medicine; medication | Toma este medicamento después de comer. | health | 3 | Take this medicine after eating.
pastilla | pill; tablet | Me tomé una pastilla para el dolor. | health | 2 | I took a pill for the pain.
dentista | dentist | Mañana tengo que ir al dentista. | health | 2 | Tomorrow I have to go to the dentist.
ambulancia | ambulance | La ambulancia llegó en cinco minutos. | health | 2 | The ambulance arrived in five minutes.
peinarse | to comb your hair; to do your hair | Mi hermana tarda mucho en peinarse. | health | 3 | My sister takes ages to do her hair.
pie | foot | Me duele el pie derecho. | health | 2 | My right foot hurts.
pierna | leg | Me duele la pierna izquierda. | health | 2 | My left leg hurts.
brazo | arm | Mi primo se rompió el brazo esquiando. | health | 2 | My cousin broke his arm skiing.
espalda | back | Tengo dolor de espalda desde ayer. | health | 2 | I've had back pain since yesterday.
estómago | stomach | Me duele el estómago. | health | 2 | I have a stomachache.
garganta | throat | Me duele la garganta desde ayer. | health | 2 | I've had a sore throat since yesterday.
cuello | neck | La jirafa tiene el cuello muy largo. | health | 2 | The giraffe has a very long neck.
rodilla | knee | Me caí de la bicicleta y me duele la rodilla. | health | 2 | I fell off my bike and my knee hurts.
dedo | finger; toe | Me corté el dedo con un cuchillo. | health | 2 | I cut my finger with a knife.
piel | skin | Hay que proteger la piel del sol. | health | 3 | You have to protect your skin from the sun.

# The home and chores
piso | floor; story (of a building) (in Spain also: apartment) | Vivimos en el tercer piso. | housing | 2 | We live on the third floor.
departamento | apartment (in Mexico, Argentina, Chile, Peru; elsewhere: apartamento) | Mis tíos alquilan un departamento en el centro. | housing | 2 | My aunt and uncle rent an apartment downtown.
alquiler | rent | El alquiler se paga el primer día del mes. | housing | 3 | The rent is paid on the first day of the month.
dueño | owner; landlord | El dueño del departamento vive arriba. | housing | 3 | The owner of the apartment lives upstairs.
vecino | neighbor; neighbour | Mi vecino pone la música muy alta. | housing | 2 | My neighbor plays his music very loud.
jardín | garden; yard | Tenemos un jardín pequeño detrás de la casa. | housing | 2 | We have a small yard behind the house.
pasillo | hallway; corridor | El baño está al final del pasillo. | housing | 2 | The bathroom is at the end of the hallway.
techo | ceiling; roof | El techo de la cocina es muy alto. | housing | 3 | The kitchen ceiling is very high.
mueble | piece of furniture | Este mueble era de mi abuela. | housing | 3 | This piece of furniture was my grandmother's.
armario | closet; wardrobe (in much of Latin America also: clóset) | El armario está lleno de ropa. | housing | 3 | The closet is full of clothes.
cajón | drawer | Las tijeras están en el primer cajón. | housing | 3 | The scissors are in the top drawer.
lavadora | washing machine | La lavadora hace mucho ruido. | housing | 2 | The washing machine makes a lot of noise.
calefacción | heating | La calefacción no funcionaba y teníamos frío. | housing | 3 | The heating wasn't working and we were cold.
luz | light; electricity; power | Anoche no hubo luz en todo el barrio. | housing | 2 | Last night there was no power in the whole neighborhood.
encender | to turn on; to light (in much of Latin America also: prender) | ¿Puedes encender la calefacción? | housing | 3 | Can you turn on the heating?
apagar | to turn off; to switch off | No olvides apagar la luz. | housing | 2 | Don't forget to turn off the light.
lavar | to wash | Tengo que lavar los platos. | housing | 2 | I have to wash the dishes.
barrer | to sweep | Ayer me tocó barrer la cocina. | housing | 3 | Yesterday it was my turn to sweep the kitchen.
planchar | to iron | Mi papá odia planchar camisas. | housing | 3 | My dad hates ironing shirts.
ordenar | to tidy (up); to put in order | Tienes que ordenar tu habitación. | housing | 2 | You have to tidy your room.
hacer la cama | to make the bed | Mi hermano nunca quiere hacer la cama. | housing | 2 | My brother never wants to make his bed.
sacar la basura | to take out the trash | Los lunes me toca sacar la basura. | housing | 2 | On Mondays it's my turn to take out the trash.
regar | to water (plants) | ¿Puedes regar las plantas este fin de semana? | housing | 3 | Can you water the plants this weekend?
limpio | clean | El baño ya está limpio. | housing | 2 | The bathroom is clean now.
sucio | dirty | Todo está muy sucio después de la fiesta. | housing | 2 | Everything is really dirty after the party.
vacío | empty | El refrigerador está casi vacío. | housing | 2 | The fridge is almost empty.
ruido | noise | Hay mucho ruido en esta calle. | housing | 2 | There's a lot of noise on this street.

# Work and jobs
trabajador | worker; hard-working | Mi tío es muy trabajador. | work | 2 | My uncle is very hard-working.
empleado | employee | El nuevo empleado empieza el lunes. | work | 2 | The new employee starts on Monday.
empleo | job; employment | Mi hermana encontró un empleo nuevo. | work | 3 | My sister found a new job.
empresa | company; firm | La empresa tiene cincuenta empleados. | work | 3 | The company has fifty employees.
negocio | business; shop | Mi tía tiene un negocio de ropa. | work | 3 | My aunt has a clothing business.
fábrica | factory | Mi abuelo trabajó en una fábrica de zapatos. | work | 3 | My grandfather worked in a shoe factory.
compañero | colleague; classmate; partner | Un compañero me ayudó mucho el primer día. | work | 2 | A colleague helped me a lot on the first day.
reunión | meeting | La reunión empezó tarde. | work | 3 | The meeting started late.
escritorio | desk | Mi escritorio está lleno de papeles. | work | 2 | My desk is covered in papers.
sueldo | salary; wages; pay | Me pagan el sueldo a fin de mes. | work | 3 | I get paid my salary at the end of the month.
turno | shift; turn | Mi mamá trabaja en el turno de noche. | work | 3 | My mom works the night shift.
profesión | profession; occupation | ¿Cuál es tu profesión? | work | 3 | What is your profession?
anuncio | ad; advertisement; announcement | Vi un anuncio de trabajo en internet. | work | 3 | I saw a job ad online.
éxito | success | La reunión fue un éxito. | work | 3 | The meeting was a success.
jubilado | retired | Mi abuelo está jubilado desde hace cinco años. | work | 3 | My grandfather has been retired for five years.
mecánico | mechanic | El mecánico arregló el carro en una hora. | work | 2 | The mechanic fixed the car in an hour.
peluquero | hairdresser; barber | El peluquero me cortó el pelo muy corto. | work | 3 | The hairdresser cut my hair very short.
periodista | journalist | Mi prima quiere ser periodista. | work | 3 | My cousin wants to be a journalist.
veterinario | vet; veterinarian | Llevamos al perro al veterinario. | work | 2 | We took the dog to the vet.
cartero | mail carrier; postman | El cartero trae las cartas por la mañana. | work | 3 | The mail carrier brings the letters in the morning.
granjero | farmer | El granjero tiene vacas y gallinas. | work | 3 | The farmer has cows and chickens.
científico | scientist | De niño quería ser científico. | work | 3 | As a child I wanted to be a scientist.

# School and studying
primaria | primary school; elementary school | Mi hermanito todavía está en primaria. | education | 2 | My little brother is still in elementary school.
secundaria | secondary school; middle or high school (in Spain: instituto) | Empecé la secundaria el año pasado. | education | 2 | I started secondary school last year.
universidad | university; college | Mi hermana estudia en la universidad. | education | 2 | My sister studies at university.
carrera | (university) degree; career; race | Mi prima terminó la carrera de medicina. | education | 3 | My cousin finished her medical degree.
curso | course; school year | Hice un curso de inglés el verano pasado. | education | 2 | I did an English course last summer.
aula | classroom | Nuestra aula está en el segundo piso. | education | 3 | Our classroom is on the second floor.
pizarra | board; blackboard (in much of Latin America: pizarrón) | La maestra escribió la fecha en la pizarra. | education | 3 | The teacher wrote the date on the board.
recreo | break; recess | En el recreo jugamos con la pelota. | education | 2 | At recess we play with the ball.
materia | (school) subject (in Spain: asignatura) | Mi materia favorita es geografía. | education | 2 | My favorite subject is geography.
historia | history; story | Mi abuelo nos contó una historia muy divertida. | education | 2 | My grandfather told us a really funny story.
geografía | geography | En geografía estudiamos los ríos de América. | education | 2 | In geography we're studying the rivers of the Americas.
ciencias | science | Tenemos clase de ciencias los martes. | education | 2 | We have science class on Tuesdays.
educación física | PE; physical education | Hoy tenemos educación física en el patio. | education | 2 | Today we have PE in the schoolyard.
ejercicio | exercise | Este ejercicio es muy difícil. | education | 2 | This exercise is very difficult.
explicar | to explain | ¿Me puedes explicar este ejercicio? | education | 2 | Can you explain this exercise to me?
repasar | to review; to go over | Esta noche voy a repasar para el examen. | education | 3 | Tonight I'm going to review for the exam.
examen | exam; test | Ayer tuve un examen de historia. | education | 2 | Yesterday I had a history exam.
aprobar | to pass (an exam) | Necesito aprobar el examen de matemáticas. | education | 3 | I need to pass the math exam.
reprobar | to fail (an exam) (in Spain: suspender) | No quiero reprobar ninguna materia. | education | 3 | I don't want to fail any subject.
nota | grade; mark; note | Saqué una buena nota en inglés. | education | 2 | I got a good grade in English.
error | mistake; error | Cometí un error en el examen. | education | 2 | I made a mistake on the exam.

# Free time and sport
tiempo libre | free time | En mi tiempo libre toco la guitarra. | leisure | 2 | In my free time I play the guitar.
pasatiempo | hobby; pastime | Mi pasatiempo favorito es dibujar. | leisure | 3 | My favorite hobby is drawing.
descansar | to rest | Después de comer me gusta descansar un rato. | leisure | 2 | After lunch I like to rest for a while.
paseo | walk; stroll; ride | Dimos un paseo por el parque. | leisure | 2 | We went for a walk in the park.
disfrutar | to enjoy | Vamos a disfrutar del fin de semana. | leisure | 3 | We're going to enjoy the weekend.
celebrar | to celebrate | Vamos a celebrar el cumpleaños de mi abuela. | leisure | 2 | We're going to celebrate my grandmother's birthday.
deporte | sport; sports | Hago deporte tres veces por semana. | leisure | 2 | I play sports three times a week.
equipo | team; equipment | Mi equipo ganó el partido del domingo. | leisure | 2 | My team won Sunday's game.
jugador | player | Es el mejor jugador del equipo. | leisure | 2 | He's the best player on the team.
partido | game; match | El partido terminó a las diez. | leisure | 2 | The game ended at ten.
gol | goal | Marqué un gol en el último minuto. | leisure | 2 | I scored a goal in the last minute.
entrenar | to train; to practice | Vamos a entrenar el sábado por la mañana. | leisure | 3 | We're going to train on Saturday morning.
estadio | stadium | El estadio estaba lleno. | leisure | 2 | The stadium was full.
gimnasio | gym | Voy al gimnasio después de clase. | leisure | 2 | I go to the gym after class.
nadar | to swim | Me gusta nadar en el mar. | leisure | 2 | I like swimming in the sea.
esquiar | to ski | Nunca aprendí a esquiar. | leisure | 3 | I never learned to ski.
patinar | to skate | Me gusta patinar en el parque. | leisure | 2 | I like skating in the park.
pescar | to fish; to go fishing | Mi abuelo me llevaba a pescar al lago. | leisure | 3 | My grandfather used to take me fishing at the lake.
museo | museum | El museo cierra los lunes. | leisure | 2 | The museum is closed on Mondays.
teatro | theater | Fuimos al teatro con la escuela. | leisure | 2 | We went to the theater with the school.
concierto | concert | Fuimos a un concierto increíble el sábado. | leisure | 2 | We went to an amazing concert on Saturday.
entrada | ticket (for a show or game); entrance | Ya compré la entrada para el concierto. | leisure | 3 | I already bought the ticket for the concert.
zoológico | zoo | Fuimos al zoológico con mis primos. | leisure | 2 | We went to the zoo with my cousins.
serie | series; TV show | Estoy viendo una serie muy buena. | leisure | 2 | I'm watching a really good series.
programa | program; show | Mi programa favorito empieza a las ocho. | leisure | 2 | My favorite show starts at eight.

# Weather and nature
nublado | cloudy | Hoy está nublado pero no llueve. | nature | 2 | It's cloudy today but it's not raining.
soleado | sunny | Fue un día soleado y tranquilo. | nature | 2 | It was a sunny, quiet day.
caluroso | hot (day, weather) | Fue un verano muy caluroso. | nature | 3 | It was a very hot summer.
fresco | cool; fresh | Por la mañana hace fresco. | nature | 2 | It's cool in the morning.
húmedo | humid; damp | El clima aquí es muy húmedo. | nature | 3 | The climate here is very humid.
seco | dry | El verano en mi pueblo es muy seco. | nature | 2 | Summer in my town is very dry.
viento | wind | Hace demasiado viento para salir en barco. | nature | 2 | It's too windy to go out on a boat.
tormenta | storm | Anoche hubo una tormenta muy fuerte. | nature | 2 | Last night there was a very strong storm.
niebla | fog | Había mucha niebla en la carretera. | nature | 3 | There was a lot of fog on the road.
nevar | to snow | Mañana va a nevar en las montañas. | nature | 2 | Tomorrow it's going to snow in the mountains.
hielo | ice | Cuidado, hay hielo en la calle. | nature | 2 | Careful, there's ice on the street.
temperatura | temperature | La temperatura bajó mucho anoche. | nature | 2 | The temperature dropped a lot last night.
pronóstico | forecast | Según el pronóstico, mañana va a llover. | nature | 3 | According to the forecast, it's going to rain tomorrow.
paraguas | umbrella | No olvides el paraguas, va a llover. | nature | 2 | Don't forget your umbrella, it's going to rain.
montaña | mountain | En invierno vamos a la montaña. | nature | 2 | In winter we go to the mountains.
lago | lake | Nadamos en el lago todo el verano. | nature | 2 | We swam in the lake all summer.
mar | sea | El mar está muy tranquilo hoy. | nature | 2 | The sea is very calm today.
costa | coast | Mis tíos viven en la costa. | nature | 2 | My aunt and uncle live on the coast.
isla | island | Pasamos una semana en una isla. | nature | 2 | We spent a week on an island.
ola | wave | Una ola enorme mojó nuestras toallas. | nature | 2 | A huge wave soaked our towels.
campo | countryside; field | Mis abuelos viven en el campo. | nature | 2 | My grandparents live in the countryside.
selva | jungle; rainforest | Vimos monos en la selva. | nature | 3 | We saw monkeys in the jungle.
paisaje | landscape; scenery | Desde la montaña, el paisaje era hermoso. | nature | 3 | From the mountain, the scenery was beautiful.
árbol | tree | Hay un árbol enorme en el parque. | nature | 2 | There's a huge tree in the park.
flor | flower | Le regalé una flor a mi mamá. | nature | 2 | I gave my mom a flower.
planta | plant | Esta planta necesita mucha agua. | nature | 2 | This plant needs a lot of water.
luna | moon | Anoche la luna estaba enorme. | nature | 2 | Last night the moon was huge.
mosquito | mosquito | Un mosquito me picó en la pierna. | nature | 2 | A mosquito bit me on the leg.
araña | spider | Hay una araña enorme en el baño. | nature | 2 | There's a huge spider in the bathroom.
mariposa | butterfly | Vimos una mariposa azul en el jardín. | nature | 2 | We saw a blue butterfly in the garden.
serpiente | snake | En la selva vimos una serpiente. | nature | 3 | In the jungle we saw a snake.

# Feelings and opinions
preocupado | worried | Estoy preocupado por el examen. | emotions | 2 | I'm worried about the exam.
asustado | scared; frightened | El perro estaba asustado por la tormenta. | emotions | 2 | The dog was scared of the storm.
emocionado | excited | Estoy muy emocionado por el viaje. | emotions | 2 | I'm really excited about the trip.
enamorado | in love | Mi hermano está enamorado de una compañera. | emotions | 3 | My brother is in love with a classmate.
harto | fed up | Estoy harto de la lluvia. | emotions | 3 | I'm fed up with the rain.
molesto | annoyed; upset | Mi papá está molesto conmigo. | emotions | 3 | My dad is annoyed with me.
avergonzado | embarrassed; ashamed (in parts of Latin America also: apenado) | Me sentí avergonzado delante de todos. | emotions | 4 | I felt embarrassed in front of everyone.
divertido | fun; funny | El viaje fue muy divertido. | emotions | 2 | The trip was a lot of fun.
amable | kind; nice | La señora de la tienda fue muy amable. | emotions | 2 | The lady at the shop was very kind.
sorpresa | surprise | La fiesta fue una sorpresa para mi mamá. | emotions | 2 | The party was a surprise for my mom.
tristeza | sadness | Sentí mucha tristeza al dejar mi escuela. | emotions | 3 | I felt very sad leaving my school.
preocuparse | to worry | No hay que preocuparse por eso. | emotions | 3 | There's no need to worry about that.
enojarse | to get angry (in Spain: enfadarse) | Mi mamá va a enojarse si llego tarde. | emotions | 3 | My mom is going to get angry if I'm late.
llorar | to cry | El bebé empezó a llorar en el avión. | emotions | 2 | The baby started crying on the plane.
reír | to laugh | Mi abuelo siempre nos hace reír. | emotions | 2 | My grandfather always makes us laugh.
sonreír | to smile | Es difícil sonreír cuando estás triste. | emotions | 3 | It's hard to smile when you're sad.
extrañar | to miss (someone) (in Spain: echar de menos) | Voy a extrañar mucho a mis amigos. | emotions | 3 | I'm going to miss my friends a lot.
creer | to believe; to think | No puedo creer lo que pasó. | emotions | 2 | I can't believe what happened.
de acuerdo | agreed; OK; in agreement | Estoy de acuerdo contigo. | emotions | 2 | I agree with you.
importante | important | Es importante beber mucha agua. | emotions | 2 | It's important to drink lots of water.
necesario | necessary | No es necesario llevar abrigo hoy. | emotions | 2 | You don't need to bring a coat today.
posible | possible | ¿Es posible cambiar la fecha del viaje? | emotions | 2 | Is it possible to change the date of the trip?
interesante | interesting | Fue un libro muy interesante. | emotions | 2 | It was a very interesting book.
diferente | different | Cada persona es diferente. | emotions | 2 | Every person is different.
maravilloso | wonderful | Pasamos un fin de semana maravilloso. | emotions | 3 | We had a wonderful weekend.
terrible | terrible; awful | Tuve un día terrible en el trabajo. | emotions | 2 | I had a terrible day at work.

# People, family and childhood
nieto | grandson; grandchild | Mi abuela tiene un nieto nuevo. | family | 2 | My grandmother has a new grandson.
sobrino | nephew | Mi sobrino cumple cinco años mañana. | family | 2 | My nephew turns five tomorrow.
pareja | partner; couple | Mi tía vive con su pareja en Lima. | family | 3 | My aunt lives with her partner in Lima.
boda | wedding | La boda de mi prima fue en mayo. | family | 2 | My cousin's wedding was in May.
casarse | to get married | Mis tíos van a casarse en junio. | family | 3 | My aunt and uncle are going to get married in June.
nacer | to be born | Mi hermanito va a nacer en abril. | family | 3 | My baby brother is going to be born in April.
crecer | to grow; to grow up | De niño, quería crecer muy rápido. | family | 3 | As a child, I wanted to grow up very fast.
vida | life | Viví toda mi vida en esta ciudad. | family | 2 | I lived my whole life in this city.
infancia | childhood | Pasé mi infancia en un pueblo pequeño. | family | 3 | I spent my childhood in a small town.
recuerdo | memory; souvenir | Tengo un recuerdo muy bonito de ese verano. | family | 3 | I have a very nice memory of that summer.
travieso | naughty; mischievous | De niño era muy travieso. | family | 3 | As a child I was very naughty.
