funcionar | to work (of machines) | Mi computadora dejó de funcionar. | technology | 3 | My computer stopped working.
roto | broken | Mi celular está roto. | technology | 2 | My phone is broken.

# Time expressions
anteayer | the day before yesterday | Volvimos de la playa anteayer. | time | 3 | We got back from the beach the day before yesterday.
pasado | last; past | El sábado pasado fuimos al cine. | time | 2 | Last Saturday we went to the movies.
vez | time (occasion) | Fue la primera vez que vi el mar. | time | 2 | It was the first time I saw the sea.
otra vez | again | Perdí las llaves otra vez. | time | 2 | I lost my keys again.
ya no | not anymore; no longer | Ya no vivo en esa casa. | time | 2 | I don't live in that house anymore.
a menudo | often | Voy a menudo a casa de mis abuelos. | time | 3 | I often go to my grandparents' house.
de vez en cuando | from time to time; every now and then | De vez en cuando comemos en un restaurante. | time | 3 | Every now and then we eat at a restaurant.
casi nunca | hardly ever | Casi nunca veo la tele. | time | 2 | I hardly ever watch TV.
normalmente | usually; normally | Normalmente me levanto a las siete. | time | 2 | I usually get up at seven.
últimamente | lately; recently | Últimamente duermo muy poco. | time | 3 | Lately I've been sleeping very little.
pronto | soon | Espero verte muy pronto. | time | 2 | I hope to see you very soon.
enseguida | right away; immediately | Espera aquí, vuelvo enseguida. | time | 3 | Wait here, I'll be right back.
más tarde | later | Te llamo más tarde. | time | 2 | I'll call you later.
a tiempo | on time; in time | Llegamos a tiempo al aeropuerto. | time | 2 | We got to the airport on time.
tardar | to take (time); to be long | ¿Cuánto vas a tardar en llegar? | time | 3 | How long will it take you to get here?
durante | during; for | Dormí durante todo el viaje. | time | 2 | I slept during the whole trip.
al principio | at first; at the beginning | Al principio no me gustaba la comida. | time | 3 | At first I didn't like the food.
entonces | then; so | Entonces decidimos volver a casa. | time | 2 | Then we decided to go back home.
por fin | finally; at last | Por fin llegaron las vacaciones. | time | 2 | At last the vacation arrived.
mediodía | noon; midday | Siempre almorzamos al mediodía. | time | 2 | We always have lunch at noon.
madrugada | early morning; the small hours | Salimos a las cinco de la madrugada. | time | 3 | We left at five in the morning.
época | time; period; era | En esa época vivíamos en el campo. | time | 3 | At that time we lived in the countryside.
fecha | date | ¿Cuál es la fecha de tu cumpleaños? | time | 2 | What's the date of your birthday?
horario | schedule; timetable; opening hours | El horario de la biblioteca cambió. | time | 3 | The library's hours changed.
costumbre | habit; custom | Leer antes de dormir es una buena costumbre. | time | 3 | Reading before bed is a good habit.

# Useful verbs
salir | to leave; to go out | Vamos a salir mañana muy temprano. | verbs | 2 | We're going to leave very early tomorrow.
regresar | to come back; to go back | Vamos a regresar a casa en tren. | verbs | 2 | We're going to go back home by train.
entrar | to go in; to come in; to enter | No se puede entrar con comida. | verbs | 2 | You can't go in with food.
caerse | to fall (down); to fall over | El niño tiene miedo de caerse de la bicicleta. | verbs | 3 | The boy is afraid of falling off his bike.
dormirse | to fall asleep | Mi hermanito tardó mucho en dormirse. | verbs | 3 | My little brother took a long time to fall asleep.
olvidar | to forget | No quiero olvidar tu cumpleaños. | verbs | 2 | I don't want to forget your birthday.
recordar | to remember; to remind | No puedo recordar su nombre. | verbs | 2 | I can't remember his name.
encontrar | to find | Es difícil encontrar un hotel barato en agosto. | verbs | 2 | It's hard to find a cheap hotel in August.
terminar | to finish; to end | Tengo que terminar la tarea antes de cenar. | verbs | 2 | I have to finish my homework before dinner.
intentar | to try | Voy a intentar llegar temprano. | verbs | 2 | I'm going to try to arrive early.
pasar | to happen; to spend (time); to pass | Me gusta pasar tiempo con mi familia. | verbs | 2 | I like spending time with my family.
dar | to give | Le voy a dar un regalo a mi madre. | verbs | 2 | I'm going to give my mother a present.
prestar | to lend | ¿Me puedes prestar tu bicicleta? | verbs | 3 | Can you lend me your bike?
contar | to tell; to count | Te voy a contar un secreto. | verbs | 2 | I'm going to tell you a secret.
enseñar | to teach; to show | Mi abuela me va a enseñar a cocinar. | verbs | 2 | My grandmother is going to teach me to cook.
repetir | to repeat | ¿Puede repetir la pregunta, por favor? | verbs | 2 | Could you repeat the question, please?
oír | to hear | No puedo oír nada con este ruido. | verbs | 2 | I can't hear anything with this noise.
sentir | to feel | Empecé a sentir frío en la montaña. | verbs | 3 | I started to feel cold on the mountain.
acompañar | to go with; to accompany | ¿Me puedes acompañar al médico? | verbs | 3 | Can you go with me to the doctor?
avisar | to let (someone) know; to warn | Tienes que avisar a tu mamá. | verbs | 3 | You have to let your mom know.
sacar | to take out; to get (a grade) | ¿Me ayudas a sacar la ropa de la maleta? | verbs | 2 | Can you help me take the clothes out of the suitcase?
tirar | to throw; to throw away | No hay que tirar papeles en la calle. | verbs | 3 | You shouldn't throw paper on the street.
arreglar | to fix; to repair | Mi papá sabe arreglar bicicletas. | verbs | 3 | My dad knows how to fix bikes.
construir | to build | Vamos a construir un castillo de arena. | verbs | 3 | We're going to build a sandcastle.
organizar | to organize | Voy a organizar una fiesta sorpresa. | verbs | 3 | I'm going to organize a surprise party.
cumplir | to turn (an age); to keep (a promise) | Mi hermana va a cumplir doce años. | verbs | 3 | My sister is going to turn twelve.
mentir | to lie (tell a lie) | No está bien mentir a tus padres. | verbs | 3 | It's not right to lie to your parents.
